      "sourceTextSha256": "fd81868d6a49004e7c9d927f6584f1bc875fa566e5197d0c120f1e6b112bcf5a",
      "text": "Day 11 · Breakfast, then meet your guide for the transfer to the airport and a flight over the Nazca Lines, vast geoglyphs visible only from the sky and believed to have had a ritual meaning linked to water. Maria Reiche, who devoted her life to studying them, introduced them to the world and saw in them a giant agricultural calendar: after your flight, you can form your own theories. Then bus from Nazca to Paracas, a protected reserve of great natural beauty and archaeological importance; check in and free time.",
